From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add the Ilitek IL97680A command-mode driver for the Pocket Duo

The bottom panel of the Retroid Pocket Duo is the Nova's Ilitek
IL97680A, run in command mode (1280x960, four lanes, RGB888, 60 and
120 Hz, DCS brightness). Our `0560` drives the Nova in video mode and
stays as it is; the Duo gets the command-mode driver from Jacob Pyke's
posting `<20261025133741.100490-3-jacob@pyk.ee>` (RetroidPocket/linux
32d07e207d8c, via armada 0105a), as its own module so the Nova is not
touched:

- panel-ilitek-il97680a-cmd.c is armada's 0105a driver with the Nova
  entry (`retroidpocket,rpnova-panel`) and its supplies dropped and the
  driver renamed; nothing else changed.
- DRM_PANEL_ILITEK_IL97680A_CMD, next to DRM_PANEL_ILITEK_IL97680A.
- The binding is the posted one (armada 0105, RetroidPocket/linux
  9bfe85be2179), unchanged. It also lists `retroidpocket,rpnova-panel`,
  the command-mode Nova compatible, which this tree does not use.

Needs `0392` (MERGE_3D on command-mode encoders).
---
